      "profile": "Local macOS arm64 production native QUIC, signed public Rust SDK EdDSA/ES256 and current bearer HTTP catch-up. First public readiness-gated activation only.",
      "assertions": [
        "Acceptance/offer-answer alone creates no start. First verified direction-appropriate public native flow atomically commits Active, immutable start and one journal row per captured present Participant.",
        "Each actual signed physical recipient independently reacquires current credential/Device/key/source/epoch/recipient-ceiling authority. The admitted recipient without any media Connection or subscription receives the same original start; a narrowed credential receives none.",
        "Forced start-journal failure rolls back flow fact, phase and journal. After storage returns the same captured real flow recovers without another datagram; original logical replay/growth cannot rewrite the start."
      ]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "u6-req-0093",
      "profile": "Local macOS arm64 production native QUIC, signed public Rust SDK EdDSA/ES256 and current bearer HTTP catch-up. First public readiness-gated activation only.",
      "assertions": [
        "Actual signed wire validates CID/SID, no connid/operation/reply envelope scope, original started_at, admitted Participant roster, actual source Connection/PID/transport and selected G.711 mu-law capabilities.",
        "Original start typed hint precedes the cursor-bearing fact on finite HTTP recovery even after explicit Session end; immutable original Active snapshot does not revive current ended state.",
        "Both signing algorithms pass captured wire/event schema checks. Shared TypeScript/Python vectors reject changed phase, Session binding, Connection scope, foreign participant, unknown transport, duplicate connection and future timestamp."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Schema93 stores immutable first-start metadata and captured Participant epochs. The first public native flow, Session Active phase and per-recipient journal insert share one transaction; private preparation cannot trigger start.",
    "Native first-start hints use bounded existing registered physical routes with fresh per-writer authorization, independent of media Connection ownership or subscriptions. The authoritative journal survives hint loss.",
    "SDK conversation catch-up recognizes scoped session.started alongside session.ended. Current Active Sessions retain media/context/provider/transition authorization and never downgrade when legacy bindings attach.",
    "The additive live-video regression now establishes actual two-way subscribed audio and waits for the public Active snapshot before upgrading. Accepted intent, actual flow and Active observations remain distinct."
  ],
